@startuml
title UML Deployment Diagram — Proposed Ubuntu 24.04 Host
top to bottom direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
actor "Sysadmin / SRE" as Admin
node "Ubuntu 24.04 Linux host" <<device>> {
  node "systemd-managed services" <<executionEnvironment>> {
    artifact "Telemetry Collector\nPython process" as Collector
    artifact "AI Inference Service\nPython process · model TBD" as Inference
    artifact "Decision & Policy Service\nPython process" as Policy
    artifact "Safety Watchdog\nPython process" as Watchdog
    artifact "Resource Manager / Actuator\nPython process · Unix socket" as Actuator
    artifact "Read-only Dashboard API\nPython process · FastAPI" as Dashboard
  }
  database "Telemetry & Read-Projection Store\nSQLite · local" as Telemetry
  database "Audit Store\nSQLite · separate append-only database" as Audit
  node "Linux kernel interfaces\nprocfs / PSI / cgroups v2" as Kernel
}
Admin --> Dashboard : read-only local HTTP GET
Collector --> Kernel : read-only telemetry
Collector --> Telemetry : accepted samples
Inference --> Telemetry : bounded evidence read
Policy --> Telemetry : context / projection
Policy --> Inference : prediction request
Policy --> Actuator : gated action request
Watchdog --> Actuator : guarded recovery request
Policy --> Audit : decision evidence
Actuator --> Audit : action evidence
Actuator --> Kernel : gated control / read-back
Dashboard --> Telemetry : read-only projection
Dashboard --> Audit : read-only audit summary
note bottom
This is a proposed single-host deployment. It uses UML device, executionEnvironment, and artifact elements and is distinct from C4 deployment view 05.
@enduml
